;; after some discussion with claude, i realised i accidentally
;; implemented dynamic scoping in my language.

;; the language isn't so pure now is it.

(define make-adder '(lambda ('n) '(lambda ('x) (+ x n))))

(define n 15)
((make-adder 5) 4)
;; returns 19

;; the fix would be trivial, when returning a list, replace all the
;; symbols with their bounded values.
